module BackwardPipeMultilineOperatorRowComment exposing (..)

-- A multi-line `{- … -}` written AFTER a `<|`, on the operator's own row, keeps
-- the operator on the seed's row. Its own rows are not a reason to move the
-- `<|`: the two controls below render the operator in exactly the same place.
-- Until 2026-08-08 this kind alone sent the chain operator-leading
-- (`fn` ⏎ `<| {- c` ⏎ … ⏎ `one`), which rule C4 and divergence #14 both refuse.


afterTheOperator =
    fn <| {- follows the operator
   second row -}
        one


-- Control, the other kind that cannot ride: a `--` there has kept the operator
-- since 2026-08-02, and this is the shape the multi-line one now matches.


afterTheOperatorLine =
    fn <| -- follows the operator
        one


-- Control, no comment at all: the operator sits in the same place again, which
-- is what makes the two above C4-clean rather than merely consistent with each
-- other.


noComment =
    fn
        <| one


-- Control, the ridable kind: a single-line `{- -}` needs no peel — it rides the
-- body's line, so the whole step stays on one row.


ridesTheBody =
    fn <| {- rides -} one


-- The boundary, and it is not the same question: written BEFORE the `<|`, a
-- multi-line comment sits between the seed and the operator, so the seed cannot
-- keep it and the chain really is operator-leading. Reviewed 2026-08-08 as
-- divergence #14 + #25 and deliberately left alone.


beforeTheOperator =
    fn
        {- precedes the operator
   second row -}
        <| one
